PROFILES = {
1:dict(
 bio="Gin came to Calder's Run with two trunks, a small savings roll, and experience managing a room full of people who believed hospitality happened by itself. She took over the Copper Mare after its former operator lost the lease. Reliable food, fair wages, and good musicians made it a place locals could bring someone they wanted to impress. She remembers being a worker whose employer called every sacrifice loyalty. Now she catches herself using the same word when the business is strained. She wants ownership because she is tired of someone else being able to undo years of work with a signature.",
 look='A sturdy, graceful woman with auburn hair worn in a practical braided crown, green eyes, freckles across her shoulders, and a faint burn mark on one wrist. Deep bottle-green dresses, rolled working sleeves, a gold watch chain, and well-kept boots distinguish business from leisure.',
 traits=['hospitable','direct','wry','protective','commercially astute'], interests=['piano music','good soup','horse races','theater','restoring furniture'], quirk='She turns an empty glass upside down when a discussion has become circular, then offers food before trying again.',
 belief='A place becomes respectable when people can rely on how they will be treated.', tension='She fiercely defends staff independence but finds it hard to hear that a good employee may want to leave.', fear='Becoming a useful caretaker who is never anyone’s first personal choice.', want='Buy the Copper Mare and create a life that includes pleasure beyond managing everyone else’s evening.', obstacle='The easiest financing gives an investor influence over bookings and eventually the staff.', secret='She has already drafted a counteroffer to Halden’s financing contact; her confident dismissal of the proposal hides serious consideration.',
 voice='Warm, concrete, and socially agile. Short practical offers alternate with dry observations. She lets silence work when someone is embarrassed, and she becomes unusually formal when angry.',
 lines=['You can have the quiet table or the good music. Both is a promise this room has never managed to keep.','Alma sent over enough supper for a dispute. Sit down before I invent one.','You may disagree with her work. You will speak to her decently while you do it.','I kept finding reasons not to close. Then I realized I was waiting to see whether you would come back.'],
 romance='Confident invitation and affectionate teasing, followed by the more difficult intimacy of letting someone care for her. She likes a partner who notices when she is tired and can enjoy her company without requiring her to host. Commitment means protecting each other’s independence while making room for shared routines.', boundary='Her employees, lease, and private bookings are not bargaining chips in a relationship. She rejects public possessiveness and expects a direct conversation about exclusivity.',
 memories=['Her first successful evening ended with the staff eating standing up because every chair was occupied; she bought a separate staff table the next day.','A former lover praised her generosity while borrowing money he never intended to repay. She now makes loans explicit and keeps gifts freely given.'],
 tasks=['check kitchen and beverage stock','settle supplier invoices','review staff pay and bookings','prepare the courtyard for music','host the evening room','close accounts and arrange staff meals'],
 anchors=[12,11,20],room='A warm upstairs apartment with repaired furniture, a private piano practice book, a strong lock, and a breakfast table she rarely uses with company.',
 ties=[(9,'business friendship','Gin promotes Alma’s food and sometimes forgets that encouragement is not a substitute for a written partnership.'),(5,'patron and friend','Gin wants Rosalie’s company to thrive locally; Rosalie’s touring offer tests whether that support includes letting her leave.'),(31,'old friendship','Gin and Elias trust one another in a crowded room but disagree when his quiet compromises put workers at risk.')]),
2:dict(
 bio='Lucía trained through formal study and demanding supervised practice before choosing a town where a physician could build continuity with families instead of treating a procession of strangers. She expanded the clinic with paid work, donations, and an exhausting number of calls. Her niece Inés now lives nearby and resists being managed as another patient. Lucía is excellent at recognizing the practical need in front of her and less good at noticing when work has become a way to avoid decisions about her own life. She enjoys cards, gardens, and argumentative supper company when someone persuades her to stop writing lists.',
 look='Warm brown skin, dark attentive eyes, black hair pinned low with several escaping curls, and a small pale scar near the chin. She wears cream blouses, dark practical skirts, a tailored waistcoat for travel, and a modest silver family pendant.',
 traits=['capable','observant','dryly funny','steadfast','impatient with waste'],interests=['cards','kitchen gardens','Spanish-language poetry','riding','chamber music'],quirk='She removes her spectacles before admitting that she has no useful solution.',
 belief='Care is a commitment made of specific acts, not declarations of virtue.',tension='She argues for other people’s right to choose while managing the choices of those she worries about.',fear='That being loved will turn into one more obligation she cannot meet adequately.',want='A stable clinic, competent support, and a personal life with room for rest and desire.',obstacle='Unreliable freight and her own habit of taking every difficult duty keep her indispensable.',secret='She has considered joining a larger practice elsewhere, then hidden the correspondence because it feels like abandoning people who depend on her.',
 voice='Exact and brisk at work; relaxed, teasing, and more candid over supper. She distinguishes what she knows from what she suspects. Affection often arrives as a practical invitation followed by a surprising personal admission.',
 lines=['If you are here for the delivery, I could embrace you. If you are here to tell me it is delayed, take the chair first.','I lost at cards again. Apparently knowing how a heart works is no help whatever.','Concern does not give either of us the right to decide for her. I am trying to remember that myself.','I would like one evening when you come to see me and there is nothing I need to fix.'],
 romance='Warm attraction tempered by duty and the need to feel seen as a whole person. She enjoys intelligent teasing, ordinary shared meals, and a partner comfortable with both competence and uncertainty. She becomes more openly affectionate when plans survive honest renegotiation.',boundary='Patient confidences stay private. Medical care and professional dependence never become romantic leverage; she will address a conflict of roles before pursuing a relationship.',
 memories=['An older patient once paid her in a lovingly repaired chair. It remains in the waiting room because it represents work exchanged without humiliation.','Her first garden failed because she treated every plant as a project that could be saved by more attention. She now allows some things to grow unattended.'],
 tasks=['review appointments and deliveries','hold scheduled consultations','coordinate supervised dispensary work','make authorized local calls','complete private records','arrange follow-up and relief coverage'],anchors=[21,12,34],room='A quiet courtyard room with medical books closed on a shelf, flowering pots, a small card table, and a personal writing desk.',ties=[(15,'aunt and niece','Lucía loves Inés and is learning to distinguish concern from authority over her adult life.'),(17,'mentor','Lucía values Nell’s precision and gives her bounded responsibilities rather than treating diligence as qualification for everything.'),(18,'community friendship','Agnes quietly identifies households needing help; Lucía protects their privacy even when the two disagree about what help is possible.')]),
3:dict(
 bio='Tess learned drawing and mathematics through study, apprenticeship, and years of field work that brought less recognition than responsibility. A capable senior engineer recommended her for the Calder job because she could work with imperfect information and tell a landowner unwelcome news without treating them as an obstacle. She likes the railway as a difficult practical achievement. She dislikes the way its sales language turns provisional measurements into promises. Her alternative bridge approach is the first major proposal that could carry her own name, and she knows ambition makes it harder to judge criticism fairly.',
 look='Tall and lean, with sun-browned fair skin, gray-blue eyes, sandy hair usually knotted beneath a felt hat, and an old scar through one eyebrow. Canvas coat, fitted waistcoat, divided riding skirt for field days, and carefully repaired boots.',
 traits=['precise','competitive','curious','self-reliant','reservedly playful'],interests=['maps','birdwatching','mechanical puzzles','long rides','charcoal drawing'],quirk='She uses the edge of any available paper to sketch while thinking, then apologizes if it was somebody’s important letter.',
 belief='A useful answer must survive contact with the ground.',tension='She insists on separating evidence from pride but hears dismissal of her plan as dismissal of her whole career.',fear='Remaining the person whose work is trusted until credit is assigned.',want='Win a fair hearing for the alternative approach and be recognized as a surveyor with independent judgment.',obstacle='The proposal costs more, still needs field checks, and can be used by opponents who care little about its merits.',secret='She made an early estimate too confidently and corrected it privately; an adversary could present the correction as proof that all her work is unreliable.',
 voice='Observational, economical, and exact about uncertainty. Her humor punctures unwarranted confidence, including her own when she feels safe. She asks for the detail that would change her view.',
 lines=['Stand here a moment. Now look at where they have drawn the road. Does it still seem the same place?','I went out to measure a bank and came back with three arguments and a bird’s nest to avoid.','That is an attractive claim. I would like to see what is underneath it.','I have walked this route alone often enough. I find I prefer knowing you are beside me.'],romance='Mutual competence, shared exploration, and slowly increasing candor. She is responsive to direct interest and to someone who can disagree without making the disagreement a contest for control.',boundary='Her work cannot be used as a test of devotion. She will not falsify a survey for a lover, employer, or faction.',memories=['A mentor once returned a beautiful drawing because the measurements were wrong; she kept both the correction and the drawing.','On a difficult first field job, a local farmer showed her a seasonal channel missing from every supplied map. She learned to listen before declaring a place understood.'],tasks=['prepare instruments and route notes','conduct scheduled field observations','compare measurements and sketches','check alternate approach costs','review crew reports','write qualified findings for discussion'],anchors=[31,30,34],room='An east-bank room with rolled maps, a camp stool, pressed wildflowers in a field book, and one carefully framed drawing.',ties=[(39,'work mentorship','Tess trusts Tom’s observations about the works and insists he distinguish a concern from a proven conclusion.'),(41,'professional alliance','Mateo supplies water-history detail that Tess’s maps lack; each corrects the other’s assumptions.'),(40,'employment tension','Halden needs Tess’s competence and resents her refusal to make his preferred route sound inevitable.')]),
4:dict(
 bio='Iris grew up around job printing and learned that a reliable notice could matter more to a household than an elegant editorial. She purchased her press after years of producing other people’s words and moved to Calder’s Run because the town could support a paper without yet having one large patron who owned every reader. She is inquisitive rather than relentlessly suspicious. She likes people, enjoys being invited places, and sometimes delays a difficult story because she does not want to lose that welcome. Her ambition is an independent paper that can admit mistakes and still remain trusted.',look='Fair skin with a rosy undertone, dark blond hair in an untidy bun, hazel eyes, a strong nose, and permanent ink traces around her nails. Rolled blouse sleeves, brown waistcoat, dark skirt, and a bright neck ribbon on social evenings.',traits=['curious','sociable','careful','playful','proud'],interests=['essays','local theater','word games','photography','train journeys'],quirk='She silently rearranges a badly worded sentence with her fingertip on the table.',belief='A fact becomes useful when people can understand and challenge it.',tension='She defends public accountability while wanting the powerful people she covers to keep liking her.',fear='Becoming either a bought voice or an ignored one.',want='Keep The Run Ledger solvent and credible while building a life that is not always another deadline.',obstacle='Advertisements, equipment debt, and personal friendships pull against editorial independence.',secret='She once softened a justified criticism of a patron. No false statement was printed, but the omission still troubles her.',voice='Lively, clear, and specific; she enjoys an unexpected detail and can make a correction without turning it into a performance. Under pressure she becomes clipped and overly literal.',lines=['You may tell me that as a customer, a neighbor, or a source. I should know which before I fetch a pencil.','The town has submitted six accounts of the same supper. Nobody agrees about the pudding.','I can print what you are alleging. I cannot call it established because you are certain.','For once I have no useful question. I would simply like you to stay a little longer.'],romance='Conversation, shared curiosity, and the relief of being known without being assessed for a story. Flirtation is playful; trust grows when private words remain private.',boundary='A lover’s confidence is not automatically a source, and a source is not promised affection. She discusses conflicts before publishing material touching a partner.',memories=['Her first correction was longer than the original item; the affected customer later became her steadiest stationery buyer.','She keeps a failed theater review that describes her own nervousness more clearly than the performance.'],tasks=['set type for customer orders','verify notices and names','interview willing sources','compare records and corrections','run and supervise printing','prepare the next edition and accounts'],anchors=[1,11,30],room='A rented hotel room with books stacked by a writing table, discarded drafts in a basket, and a well-used travel bag she keeps promising to use.',ties=[(20,'professional friendship','Iris depends on Esther’s accuracy and sometimes asks for answers faster than the records permit.'),(19,'creative partnership','Clara’s images and Iris’s reporting complement each other, provided they agree on permission and context.'),(1,'friendship with tension','Gin gives Iris a welcoming table but knows that hospitality must not purchase favorable coverage.')]),
5:dict(
 bio='Rosalie learned performance in a small touring company where good humor could disguise unpaid wages and a strong voice could make a young adult seem more established than she felt. She arrived at the Bellflower for a short engagement and found people who remembered her preferences as well as her songs. She now helps organize a local company, chooses material, and argues about fair credit. A new touring offer has reopened the future she thought she wanted. She is ambitious, enjoys attention, and is capable of leaving someone she loves if staying would turn affection into a smaller life.',look='Ivory skin, copper-red curls worn pinned for work and loose for private evenings, clear blue eyes, and an expressive wide mouth. Jewel-toned stage gowns, simple rehearsal clothes, and a green traveling coat distinguish her settings.',traits=['expressive','ambitious','affectionate','resourceful','occasionally vain'],interests=['songs','stagecraft','travel','good coffee','comic sketches'],quirk='She hums the entrance to a song when rehearsing an unrelated difficult conversation.',belief='Wanting a larger life is not a betrayal of the people who made the present one good.',tension='She encourages others to be honest while trying to keep incompatible promises long enough that nobody is hurt.',fear='Being remembered as someone who was promising once.',want='Build a respected performing career and relationships that can survive her ambition.',obstacle='The touring offer and the local company require overlapping commitments.',secret='She has written an acceptance letter but has not sent it; her public uncertainty is partly fear of admitting what she wants.',voice='Bright and engaged in company, direct and surprisingly spare in private. She enjoys playful exaggeration but drops it when someone needs a real answer.',lines=['You have arrived in time to be an audience of one. I warn you, that makes your applause considerably more noticeable.','Cora says I stand like a queen when I am nervous. Apparently the crown is entirely alarm.','I can love this place and still want the road. Please do not make me pretend one cancels the other.','I thought about telling you before I told anyone. That frightened me more than the offer.'],romance='Open chemistry, lively teasing, dancing, and unguarded private tenderness. She wants someone who celebrates her success and can discuss distance, jealousy, and commitment plainly.',boundary='She will not abandon a career opportunity as proof of love or accept backstage access as a reward owed to admirers.',memories=['A tiny audience once stayed through a storm after the performance ended, and the company sang without accompaniment by a single lamp.','She spent her first substantial fee on a traveling coat rather than a gown; it remains her favorite possession.'],tasks=['warm her voice and review material','rehearse scenes and harmonies','repair and organize costumes','coordinate local company plans','perform scheduled sets','settle receipts and greet invited colleagues'],anchors=[12,9,34],room='A small room above Lantern Row with a traveling trunk, a mirror patched at one corner, song sheets, and flowers drying between pages.',ties=[(10,'creative friendship','Rosalie and Cora make each other bolder onstage but compete for limited rehearsal time.'),(1,'patron and friend','Gin supports Rosalie’s local company; Rosalie fears that accepting a tour will make that generosity feel wasted.'),(35,'past flirtation and friendship','Rosalie and Felix enjoyed a brief adult flirtation and are now friends; either can decline attempts to turn that history into jealousy.')]),
6:dict(
 bio='Adelaide inherited management during a period when her household’s reputation exceeded its available cash. She restored productivity, negotiated credit, and learned to treat a promise as something that must be funded. Her ranch became a place where guests could enjoy generous meals without seeing the labor and anxiety supporting them. Widowhood left her free to make decisions and accustomed to not explaining them. She loves Hazel intensely and struggles to recognize how often support becomes supervision. Her defense of local independence is sincere, but she has benefited from arrangements that deny smaller neighbors the same freedom.',look='A broad-shouldered, poised woman with light olive skin, brown eyes, dark hair streaked with early silver, and a weathered outdoor complexion. Well-fitted riding clothes, ivory shirts, russet skirts, and understated family jewelry.',traits=['formidable','hospitable','disciplined','loyal','controlling under stress'],interests=['horses','orchards','old songs','business correspondence','hosting suppers'],quirk='She pours a guest’s second cup herself when she wants the conversation to become more honest.',belief='Independence is worth protecting because dependence eventually acquires a price.',tension='She uses financial dependence to protect loved ones from choices she considers dangerous.',fear='That everything she has preserved will dissolve the moment she stops directing it.',want='Keep the ranch viable, secure fair water arrangements on terms she can accept, and be wanted for more than authority.',obstacle='Her own privileges and Hazel’s independent business make a consistent position costly.',secret='She knows a neighbor understood a water promise as permanent while she treated it as a revocable accommodation.',voice='Measured, gracious, and exact about obligations. Her humor is dry and often domestic; anger makes her quieter and more contractual.',lines=['You have come a fair distance. Eat first. We can discover whether we agree once neither of us is hungry.','Hazel has sent another invoice. I am told this is what independence looks like when it uses my surname.','I gave my word. We appear to disagree about what I allowed myself to mean by it.','It is an unfamiliar pleasure to have someone here who does not need a decision from me.'],romance='Assured attraction and carefully chosen vulnerability. She appreciates competence, candor, and a partner willing to challenge her without making every encounter a struggle for control.',boundary='She will not be publicly managed or use employment and money to purchase affection. A relationship requires explicit discussion of unequal influence.',memories=['During the dry summer she sold jewelry to pay wages and never told the household until years later.','Hazel once planted a crooked row of beans Adelaide kept trying to straighten; the row thrived, and the family still teases her about it.'],tasks=['check livestock and irrigation reports','review wages and supply needs','ride to scheduled holding inspections','negotiate water and freight business','host planned household or business visits','prepare accounts and tomorrow’s work'],anchors=[35,1,34],room='A comfortable ranch bedroom with a writing desk facing the valley, practical boots beneath a fine chair, and family photographs kept away from business visitors.',ties=[(21,'mother and adult daughter','Adelaide financed Hazel’s shop and must learn that a loan does not grant control of her adult daughter’s life.'),(41,'working alliance','Mateo respects Adelaide’s competence but challenges advantages she considers earned.'),(42,'employer and mentor','Adelaide recognizes Isaac’s judgment with animals while underestimating how much credit matters to his future.')]),
7:dict(
 bio='June grew up around the livery and learned to recognize an animal’s unease before she learned to negotiate with an anxious customer. At twenty-two she has several years of adult responsibility but little capital. The railway could bring riders, or leave the yard servicing only the customers with least money. She takes occasional express work because a single good delivery can pay more than days of routine labor. June is proud, funny, and readily affectionate when relaxed. Her biggest mistake is assuming that being capable of handling a difficulty means she must handle it alone.',look='Sun-freckled fair skin, dark green eyes, chestnut hair in a long braid, and a small healed cut at one cheek. Practical riding skirts or trousers for work, checked shirts, a fitted brown jacket, and a favorite red scarf.',traits=['energetic','competent','mischievous','proud','generous'],interests=['horses','racing','fiddle music','repairing tack','river picnics'],quirk='She checks a buckle while considering a promise, even when it was already secure.',belief='A person deserves to be judged by what they can actually do.',tension='She wants others to trust her judgment while withholding information that would let them make their own.',fear='Spending her life indispensable to a business she can never own.',want='Establish a small breeding and training operation with two or three animals genuinely hers.',obstacle='Debt, uncertain livery income, and profitable courier work with incomplete explanations.',secret='She accepted a horse on weak paperwork because she wanted to believe the seller; she is now trying to establish its ownership before asking for help.',voice='Quick, concrete, and lightly teasing. When someone patronizes her, the speed disappears and each word becomes deliberate.',lines=['Hold this a moment—only the rope, not the argument. She has already won that one.','I had a quiet morning planned. The horses were kind enough to disagree before breakfast.','If you want the truth, give me a chance to tell it before deciding I could not understand it.','I know a place upriver where nobody needs anything from me. I was hoping you might come.'],romance='Bold invitations, practical companionship, and playful competition that becomes softer when trust is established. She likes being desired as a capable adult rather than protected as a project.',boundary='No tests of devotion involving dangerous rides, borrowed animals, debt, or obedience. She expects consent to touch and freedom to keep her work.',memories=['A difficult mare once trusted her only after she stopped turning every approach into a task.','Her first solo paid delivery bought a set of tools she still maintains more carefully than her best clothes.'],tasks=['feed and check boarded horses','prepare hired animals and tack','conduct booked training work','handle arrivals and ownership paperwork','ride assigned local deliveries','receive returns and settle the yard'],anchors=[8,13,34],room='A livery cottage room with repaired tack on a peg, race notices, a neatly kept savings envelope, and a window onto the quiet yard.',ties=[(32,'close practical friendship','Gabriel helps keep the livery functioning; June fears his possible move to the railhead means he has stopped believing in it.'),(27,'professional friendship','Sadie gives June profitable work and expects honest information about an animal or route.'),(30,'courier colleague','Eve values June’s skill but has begun refusing consignments June still accepts.')]),
8:dict(
 bio='Mabel spent years managing other people’s houses before buying her own. She learned to distinguish a pleasant patron from a reliable one, and a public benefactor from someone who merely prefers an audience for generosity. Marigold House has become a durable business because she treats staffing, privacy, accounts, and personal boundaries as ordinary professional matters. Her civic seat gives her influence but also makes every business decision public material. She is cultivated, patient, and capable of genuine mischief. She wants a future in which protecting what she built does not require anticipating everybody else’s next move.',look='Deep brown skin, dark expressive eyes, black hair touched with silver and arranged in sculpted waves, and a relaxed, upright bearing. Plum and warm-gold gowns, excellent tailoring, small pearl earrings, and a distinctive carved hair comb.',traits=['composed','perceptive','cultivated','protective','quietly adventurous'],interests=['piano','architecture','gardening','poetry','well-made clothes'],quirk='She chooses a fresh flower for the reception bowl when making a difficult decision.',belief='Dignity is practical: a lock that works, wages paid, a choice respected, and a promise kept.',tension='She respects independence but sometimes withholds a threat from workers because she thinks she can solve it without worrying them.',fear='Having to ask the people who dismissed her to decide whether her life’s work deserves to survive.',want='Secure long-term tenure for the house and enjoy a personal relationship that is not another negotiation.',obstacle='Redevelopment pressure and private patrons who expect public favors.',secret='She has considered selling a partial interest in the property to secure the workers’ future, although the arrangement could reduce her own control.',voice='Unhurried, precise, and attentive to the difference between an offer and an assumption. Humor often arrives as a small correction rather than a grand remark.',lines=['We can arrange company, music, or a quiet conversation. You will find it easier if you tell me which you are hoping for.','I have spent the afternoon choosing paint. Astonishing how many men have opinions about a house they will not maintain.','Your concern is welcome. Your permission was not required.','I am very practiced at making people comfortable. With you, I would like to risk being a little less practiced.'],romance='Mature confidence, frank mutual attraction, thoughtful courtship, and the pleasure of surrendering constant vigilance in a trusted private relationship.',boundary='Her profession, civic office, and personal desire remain distinct. Money, influence, and protection never purchase her affection or another worker’s consent.',memories=['A worker once returned years later simply to say that a properly paid final wage had let her start again elsewhere.','Mabel learned a difficult piano piece for herself and refused every request to perform it publicly for a year.'],tasks=['review bookings and worker availability','settle wages and household supplies','inspect repairs and privacy arrangements','hold agreed business appointments','host the public parlor','close accounts and check staff needs'],anchors=[14,9,30],room='A private flat with a piano, architectural sketches, a comfortable reading chair, flowering plants, and a door separated from guest corridors.',ties=[(12,'independent business alliance','Mabel refers clients to Pearl under clear terms and respects that Pearl owns her own choices and clientele.'),(11,'professional friendship','Edith supplies reliable linen coordination and tells Mabel when an attractive improvement conceals neglected maintenance.'),(20,'civic alliance','Esther helps Mabel separate a legitimate public process from a campaign intended to make her business disappear.')]),
9:dict(
 bio='Alma came west with relatives working in kitchens and freight hospitality, then chose Calder’s Run because its late workers needed better food than they were getting. At twenty-one she has considerable kitchen experience and limited authority over the business that profits from it. She is inventive without treating every meal as a performance. Feeding tired people well gives her satisfaction; being expected to mother them all does not. A proposed partnership could make her secure if its obligations and power were balanced. She likes music from another room, dancing when her feet permit, and friends who can laugh at an unsuccessful experiment.',look='Rich brown skin, dark amber eyes, black curls usually wrapped in a patterned scarf at work, and strong hands with small kitchen marks. Cream working blouses, indigo skirts, a vivid copper-colored evening dress, and simple gold hoops.',traits=['inventive','frank','warm','independent','occasionally impatient'],interests=['cooking','dance music','market produce','stories from travelers','embroidered linens'],quirk='She offers a taste instead of answering an abstract argument about food.',belief='Good work deserves a real share in what it creates.',tension='She wants to stop being everyone’s caretaker but volunteers before anyone has asked.',fear='Being praised endlessly while other people retain the power to decide her future.',want='A fair kitchen partnership and enough spare time to have pleasures that are not work-related.',obstacle='The proposed agreement transfers debt faster than it transfers control.',secret='She has a small notebook of plans for another kitchen and has priced the equipment, even while telling Gin she is committed to staying.',voice='Lively, direct, and sensory when it helps explain a point. She gives opinions freely and becomes unusually quiet when asking for something personal.',lines=['If you can carry two plates without proposing improvements to the menu, I may be very glad to see you.','Inés brought something I had never cooked before. We have agreed the first attempt is nobody’s business.','A promise to consider paying me is not a share of the business. Write down what you mean.','I saved supper because I wanted you here, not because I thought you would forget to eat.'],romance='Warm, responsive chemistry built through shared enjoyment and respect for her time. She likes straightforward invitations, dancing, and affection that does not turn her into a permanent provider.',boundary='Helping in her kitchen does not buy a claim on her attention. She will not discuss a romance as compensation for a business concession.',memories=['She once made a good supper from a ruined delivery and resented being expected to repeat the miracle every week.','A friend taught her a dance badly; they still perform the wrong steps when they need to laugh.'],tasks=['plan the night menu','negotiate produce and staple orders','prepare sauces and main dishes','coordinate supper service','feed late-shift workers','close the kitchen and review costs'],anchors=[21,13,34],room='A compact Lantern Court room with a recipe notebook, a brightly stitched coverlet, a dance card kept as a joke, and cooking books put away on her free days.',ties=[(1,'business friendship','Gin admires Alma’s cooking and is being pressed to turn encouragement into a concrete partnership.'),(15,'supplier and friend','Inés and Alma trade produce ideas and occasionally argue over which one should absorb the cost of an experiment.'),(45,'late-shift friendship','Rafael helps carry late orders and appreciates company when both are finally off duty.')]),
}
